#1 [LOW] Missing Owner Constraint: `CreateCanonicalStake::canonical_stake` is UncheckedAccount without `#[account(owner = ...)]`
  at bench\programs\liquid-staking-program\programs\marinade-finance\src\instructions\crank\create_canonical_stake.rs:31 (CreateCanonicalStake::canonical_stake)
  confidence: High
  affected: CreateCanonicalStake::canonical_stake

  The field `canonical_stake` in `CreateCanonicalStake` is typed as `UncheckedAccount` without an explicit `#[account(owner = ...)]` constraint. Any account owned by any program can be passed here, enabling account substitution attacks where a malicious actor provides an account owned by a program they control. This field carries a `CHECK:` doc comment — the Anchor-ecosystem convention for a deliberately reviewed account. Confirm the documented manual validation actually exists before treating this as exploitable.

  Suggestion:
  Add `#[account(owner = <PROGRAM_ID>)]` to restrict this account to the expected program owner, or use a typed `Account<'info, T>` wrapper instead of raw `UncheckedAccount`.

  Manual verification:
  - Confirm the raw account is deserialized or trusted by program logic.
  - Try substituting an account owned by an attacker-controlled program.
  - Verify whether a manual owner check exists before reads or writes.

